# SECTION 05 — ARCHITECTURAL CONTEXT

## Architectural Context

The Institutional Workspace Architecture defines how the COREI Workbench assembles operational capabilities into complete professional working environments.

A workspace is not merely a visual arrangement.

It is an executable operational environment that combines:

* institutional objective,
* operator context,
* governed capabilities,
* operational workflows,
* environmental state,
* runtime services,
* institutional intelligence.

The Workspace Architecture therefore becomes the composition architecture of COREI.

