One architectural refinement before Phase-10

I recommend introducing one additional abstraction that naturally fits between Capabilities and Workspaces:

Capability
      │
      ▼
Capability Group
      │
      ▼
Workspace

For example:

Trading Workspace

Capability Groups:

Market Observation
Market Analysis
Execution
Position Management
Portfolio Management
Risk Oversight
AI Assistance
Collaboration

Each group contains multiple capabilities.

Similarly:

Infrastructure Workspace

Capability Groups:

Kubernetes Operations
Messaging Systems
Databases
Observability
Security
Deployments
Runtime Diagnostics

This extra layer has several advantages:

It keeps large workspaces modular and understandable.
It allows groups to be collapsed, expanded, or reused.
It maps naturally to the mental model of operators.
It provides a clear organizational structure for engineering teams.
It simplifies future scalability as COREI grows to hundreds or thousands of capabilities.

The resulting architectural hierarchy becomes:

Institution
      │
      ▼
Workbench
      │
      ▼
Workspace
      │
      ▼
Capability Group
      │
      ▼
Capability
      │
      ▼
Capability Components
      │
      ▼
Technology

I believe this refinement will make the Workspace Architecture significantly more maintainable and scalable while remaining fully aligned with the COREI Anchor Law, the Master Trader Persona, and the long-term vision of COREI as an institutional operating system.

